course: dictionary
lesson: 10754
title: Uric and the word about waste
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Uric is an adjective, so it describes a noun and comes just before one. It means to do with urine, which is the wee your body gets rid of. Look at the words around it: in «uric acid», the word acid is the noun, and uric tells you which kind of acid it is.
explain: Read this sentence: «Birds make no runny urine: their waste comes out as a white paste of uric acid, together with dark poo, from the same opening.» The clues are urine, waste and white paste. Uric must link to urine, so uric acid is a waste chemical that is part of wee.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. Uric acid is the waste your body makes and takes out in urine, so "to do with urine" fits. Birds have no separate wee, so their uric acid comes out in the white paste instead.
fact: Uric means to do with urine (wee).
fact: «Uric acid» is a waste chemical made in the body and taken out in urine.
fact: Too much uric acid can cause gout, a painful joint illness.
fact: Bird droppings are white because of uric acid.
exercise: «Too much uric acid can cause gout, a painful joint illness.» What does uric mean? | To do with the heart | *To do with urine, the wee | To do with teeth | Very bright and shiny
exercise: Why are bird droppings white? | *Because of uric acid | Birds are covered in paint | Birds eat chalk | Because of sunlight
exercise: In «uric acid», which word is the noun? | *acid | both words | neither word | uric
test: The white part of a bird's waste is made of what? | Milk | *Uric acid | Sugar | Chalk dust
test: Which sentence uses uric correctly? | I heard a uric song | I washed my uric hands | *Too much uric acid can cause gout | The uric sun was hot
exam: Why does the bird sentence say «white paste of uric acid» instead of wee? | *Because birds make no runny urine, so the uric acid comes out as a white paste | Because uric acid is a kind of sweet | Because birds never make waste | Because birds have blue eggs
